{% macro method(workload, runs, resamples) -%}
- **Load:** a closed loop. At concurrency *k*, *k* clients each send a request and, as soon as its reply arrives, their next one. Measured at concurrency {{ workload.levels | listing }}.
- **Requests:** {{ (runs.clean * runs.requests) | num(0) }} per concurrency level: {{ runs.requests | num(0) }} in each of {{ "separate server start" | plural(runs.clean) }}{% if workload.levels | length > 1 %}, each of which measures every level in turn{% endif %}. Each level begins with {{ "unmeasured warmup request" | plural(runs.warmups) }}.
- **Latency:** the client's time from sending a request to parsing its reply, over a new loopback HTTP connection per request.
- **Throughput:** measured requests per second, from the first one's send to the last one's reply in each server start.
- **Ranges** in parentheses are 95% confidence intervals, from a bootstrap that resamples the server starts and then the requests within each ({{ resamples | num(0) }} resamples){% if runs.clean == 1 %}; with one server start, they leave out the variation between starts{% endif %}.
{%- endmacro %}

